-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This application downloads the following AI models from Hugging Face Hub
at first launch. Each model is subject to its own license:

  openai/clip-vit-base-patch32
    License: MIT
    https://huggingface.co/openai/clip-vit-base-patch32

  facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h
    License: Apache 2.0
    https://huggingface.co/facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h

On Linux and Windows, this application can download one of these pre-built
ffmpeg/ffprobe artifacts provided by yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds:

    ffmpeg-master-latest-linux64-gpl.tar.xz
    ffmpeg-master-latest-linuxarm64-gpl.tar.xz
    ffmpeg-master-latest-win64-gpl.zip

These are GNU General Public License version 3 (GPLv3) variants. The upstream
GPL build definition enables `--enable-gpl --enable-version3` and packages
FFmpeg's `COPYING.GPLv3` as `LICENSE.txt` in each artifact:
    https://github.com/yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds
    https://github.com/yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds/blob/master/variants/defaults-gpl.sh
    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html
    https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html

On macOS, this application does not download or redistribute ffmpeg. Users
provide their own ffmpeg/ffprobe installation; its license and provenance are
those of the selected installation source.

For Rust crate dependencies, see Cargo.lock and the individual crates'
license files (available via `cargo license` or on crates.io).
